# Copy to server/.env and fill in your own Stripe *test* secret key.
# Get it from https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# Optional. Needed for `stripe listen` to write completed gifts to the local ledger.
# Create the endpoint with:
#   stripe listen --forward-to localhost:4242/stripe-webhook --events payment_intent.succeeded
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me

# Optional. Emails the band each time a donation is confirmed — sandbox gifts
# included, because this server sends the mail itself.
# Needs 2-Step Verification on the Google account, then a 16-character App
# Password from https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (paste it without spaces).
# Google withholds App Passwords on some newer accounts — if so, leave Gmail empty
# and use the relay below instead; that works on its own.
# GMAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=abcdefghijklmnop
# DONATION_NOTIFY_TO=you@gmail.com   # Optional. Defaults to GMAIL_USER
#
# Anything that fails to send is retried on a backoff (1m, 5m, 15m, 1h, then
# every 6h) and kept in server/data/pending-alerts.jsonl until it goes out, so a
# mail outage delays an alert instead of losing it.

# Optional. A free SMTP relay. It can be the *only* sender: with no Gmail block
# filled in, the relay sends every alert on its own. Any plain SMTP relay works;
# verified against Brevo (smtp-relay.brevo.com:587, 300 emails/day free) and
# Mailjet (in-v3.mailjet.com:587, 200 emails/day free).
#
# Brevo, in particular:
#   * SMTP_FALLBACK_USER is the Login shown on Brevo's SMTP page, which is NOT
#     always your account email — it can look like <id>@smtp-brevo.com.
#     A wrong login and a wrong key both answer "535 Authentication failed".
#   * SMTP_FALLBACK_PASSWORD is the *SMTP key* (Settings -> SMTP & API -> SMTP),
#     not the API key and not the account password.
#   * The sender address must be verified first, under Senders.
#   * Brevo blocks unknown IP addresses by default on accounts created after
#     16 May 2024 ("525 5.7.1 Unauthorized IP address"). Authorise the sending
#     machine under Settings -> Security -> Authorized IPs, or turn it off. A
#     deployed server has a different outbound IP and needs the same treatment.
#
# Check the setup at any time without sending anything:
#   npm run check-mail             (run inside server/)
#   npm run check-mail -- --send   to deliver a real test alert
# SMTP_FALLBACK_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# SMTP_FALLBACK_PORT=587
# SMTP_FALLBACK_USER=<id>@smtp-brevo.com
# SMTP_FALLBACK_PASSWORD=xsmtpsib-your-smtp-key
# SMTP_FALLBACK_FROM=you@gmail.com    # Optional. Defaults to GMAIL_USER
# SMTP_FALLBACK_SECURE=false          # Set true for port 465
# PENDING_ALERTS_FILE=C:\path\to\pending-alerts.jsonl

# Optional overrides.
# PORT=4242
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-live-site.example
# DONATIONS_FILE=C:\path\to\donations.jsonl
